# uv
# uv.lock is deliberately NOT tracked. uv cannot see `[tool.poetry.dependencies]`
# without a PEP 621 `[project]` table, so the lock only ever covered the dev
# group -- it looked like the project's lock while pinning none of the packages
# the collector actually runs on. poetry.lock is the real one. `uv run` still
# regenerates this file locally, which is fine; it just must not be committed.
uv.lock

# Poetry
# poetry.lock is deliberately tracked: this is an application, not a library,
# and the daily release installs from requirements-collector.txt, which is
# generated from the lock. An untracked lock meant nothing was pinned -- CI
# re-resolved on every run, so a dependency could change under the collector
# between a green PR and that night's release.
.poetry/

